    <!-- Legal and help -->
    <string name="privacy_policy_title">Privacy Policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_body">SafeHer stores your account, profile, guardians, history and recordings only on this phone, in the app\'s private storage. There is no SafeHer server and nothing is uploaded.\n\nWhen you trigger an SOS, SafeHer sends a text message from your SIM to the guardians you added. It contains your first name and, if available, your location. Your medical details are never included.\n\nPasswords are stored only as salted PBKDF2 hashes. Uninstalling the app or clearing its data permanently deletes everything.</string>
    <string name="terms_title">Terms and Conditions</string>
    <string name="terms_body">SafeHer is a personal safety aid, not an emergency service. It cannot guarantee that alerts are delivered, that a location is accurate, or that anyone responds.\n\nSMS alerts depend on your mobile network, balance and signal, and normal charges may apply. In immediate danger, call 15 or 1122.\n\nOnly add guardians who have agreed to receive your alerts. Use evidence recording in line with the law where you are.</string>
    <string name="help_title">How SafeHer works</string>
    <string name="help_body">SOS: press and hold the red button for 2 seconds. A countdown lets you cancel. Then SafeHer saves a record, looks for your location and texts your guardians.\n\nGuardians: add trusted people with their phone numbers. Tell them you\'ve added them — SafeHer does not.\n\nSafe Journey: set a destination and arrival time, and tap I\'ve arrived when you get there.\n\nFake Call: schedule a pretend incoming call to help you leave a situation.</string>

